WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:04.810
Welcome to Lab one of the Azure AI Gateway labs.

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.010
In three minutes, you'll provision your own gateway from the portal,

3
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:13.010
find its runtime URL and managed identity, and learn where everything lives.

4
00:00:13.653 --> 00:00:15.333
Here's what provisioning does.

5
00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:18.693
You choose a name, a resource group, and a region.

6
00:00:18.693 --> 00:00:25.013
Azure creates a connector gateway, then the AI Gateway, with a system-assigned managed identity.

7
00:00:25.013 --> 00:00:29.213
You get back one runtime URL for every app and agent.

8
00:00:29.861 --> 00:00:35.821
In the AI Gateway portal, open the gateway switcher at the top, and choose Create new gateway.

9
00:00:36.431 --> 00:00:40.031
The dialog suggests a unique name and confirms it's available.

10
00:00:40.031 --> 00:00:42.671
Select refresh to generate another.

11
00:00:42.671 --> 00:00:47.991
The name becomes part of your runtime URL, so keep it to twenty-four characters or fewer.

12
00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:53.555
Pick your subscription, and create a new resource group, or reuse an existing one.

13
00:00:53.555 --> 00:00:55.155
Then choose a region.

14
00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:59.515
During the preview, that's East US 2 or Sweden Central.

15
00:01:00.184 --> 00:01:01.864
Expand Advanced.

16
00:01:01.864 --> 00:01:05.464
The system-assigned managed identity is on by default.

17
00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:06.504
Keep it.

18
00:01:06.504 --> 00:01:10.344
The gateway uses it to reach Foundry and other Entra-protected backends,

19
00:01:10.344 --> 00:01:13.024
so your apps never hold provider keys.

20
00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:16.697
Under Networking, keep public routing for this lab.

21
00:01:16.697 --> 00:01:20.937
Private routing reaches private backends through secure outbound connections,

22
00:01:20.937 --> 00:01:23.537
and it can't be changed after creation.

23
00:01:24.181 --> 00:01:26.021
Select Create gateway.

24
00:01:26.021 --> 00:01:32.181
All gateways tracks progress live: creating the resource group, deploying, then activating.

25
00:01:32.181 --> 00:01:38.221
About a minute and a half later, it shows Succeeded, with the runtime URL right in the list.

26
00:01:38.859 --> 00:01:41.419
Home now shows your new gateway in the switcher.

27
00:01:41.419 --> 00:01:46.299
The setup guide lists what's next: add a model, test it, and apply policies.

28
00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:48.339
That's where lab two picks up.

29
00:01:48.995 --> 00:01:50.435
A quick tour.

30
00:01:50.435 --> 00:01:53.395
Discover is the catalog developers browse.

31
00:01:53.395 --> 00:01:56.355
Models and MCP servers are what you publish.

32
00:01:56.355 --> 00:02:00.355
Access holds Entra ID role assignments and API keys.

33
00:02:00.355 --> 00:02:02.515
Policies are your guardrails.

34
00:02:02.515 --> 00:02:06.275
Monitoring shows usage, cost, and traces.

35
00:02:06.275 --> 00:02:09.355
And Networking is read-only after creation.

36
00:02:10.103 --> 00:02:11.703
Open Managed identities.

37
00:02:11.703 --> 00:02:14.343
The system-assigned identity is enabled, with its principal ID.

38
00:02:14.343 --> 00:02:20.983
In later labs, you grant it access to Foundry, so the gateway authenticates outbound for you.

39
00:02:21.749 --> 00:02:23.269
Now verify from a terminal.

40
00:02:23.269 --> 00:02:27.589
Read the host name from the resource, then call a model route without a key.

41
00:02:27.589 --> 00:02:30.229
HTTP 404 is what you want.

42
00:02:30.229 --> 00:02:33.509
DNS, TLS, and the gateway all answer.

43
00:02:33.509 --> 00:02:35.789
There are simply no models yet.

44
00:02:36.365 --> 00:02:37.765
Prefer automation?

45
00:02:37.765 --> 00:02:41.285
A single Azure CLI call creates the AI gateways resource.

46
00:02:41.285 --> 00:02:45.605
Or use a short Bicep file that outputs the URL and principal ID.

47
00:02:45.605 --> 00:02:48.765
The lab includes both, plus a Jupyter notebook.

48
00:02:49.429 --> 00:02:52.509
Keep this gateway, because every later lab reuses it.

49
00:02:52.509 --> 00:02:55.389
When you finish the labs, delete the resource group.

50
00:02:55.389 --> 00:02:57.589
Next up: lab two.
